<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shona</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shona are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a> and neighbouring areas. They formed the population of states such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zimbabwe">Great Zimbabwe</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a>. Accounts of the Rozvi Empire describe the predominantly Shona-speaking population as a source of agricultural tribute.</p></div>
